<title>BELGIUM: FLANDERS GOVT SUPPORTS PICANOL PLAN.</title>
<headline>FLANDERS GOVT SUPPORTS PICANOL PLAN.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The regional government of Flanders said on Tuesday it would lend financial support to an 801 million Belgian franc investment programme by Belgian textile machinery maker Picanol NV.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Flanders' Economics Minister Eric Van Rompuy said the government's share in the investment would be 38 million Belgian francs.</p>
<p>In a statement, the government said a quarter of Picanol's planned investment would be on research and development. The balance would be aimed at producing a new range of looms.</p>
<p>The workforce will increase by 24 to 1,260.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
